{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"general"},"prompt":"Write a haiku-style poem of exactly three nonempty lines about a rainy morning. Mention or clearly evoke both rain and morning. Output only the three lines and nothing else.","ground_truth":{"type":"constraint_based","requirements":["Output contains exactly three nonempty lines and no title, commentary, or surrounding text.","The poem clearly evokes a rainy morning.","The text is a concise haiku-style poem."],"acceptable_examples":["Rain taps windowpanes\nDawn gathers in silver pools\nSparrows shake their wings"]},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_rubric","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_three_nonempty_lines","regex":"^\\s*\\S[^\\n]*\\n\\s*\\S[^\\n]*\\n\\s*\\S[^\\n]*\\s*$"}],"semantic_rubric":{"required":["Clearly evokes rain or rainy weather.","Clearly evokes morning, dawn, or an equivalent early-day setting.","Is a concise poem rather than prose, metadata, or an explanation."],"fail_if":["Contains commentary outside the poem.","Does not address a rainy morning."]}}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["unit_test_required"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L1.002","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"form":"recipe","audience_specificity":"general"},"prompt":"Write a recipe for lemonade with exactly three numbered steps. Put each step on a separate line beginning exactly with \"1.\", \"2.\", and \"3.\" in that order. Do not include a title, ingredients list, or any other text. Output only the three steps.","ground_truth":"1. Squeeze lemons into a pitcher and remove any seeds.\n2. Stir the lemon juice with water and sugar until the sugar dissolves.\n3. Add ice, taste, and serve the lemonade cold.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_semantic_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_three_numbered_lines","regex":"\\A\\s*1\\.[^\\n]+\\n2\\.[^\\n]+\\n3\\.[^\\n]+\\s*\\Z"},{"name":"lemonade_recipe_semantics","criterion":"All three lines collectively describe making lemonade, including lemon or lemon juice and plausible preparation actions; the response contains no title, ingredient list, commentary, or additional steps."}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L1.003","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"general"},"prompt":"Write a free-verse poem about the night sky. The poem must have exactly six lines. Output only the six lines.","ground_truth":"开放式参考标准：接受任意原创自由诗，只要输出仅包含恰好六个非空行（不含标题、编号、解释或额外空行），且六行整体明确描绘或表达夜空，例如星星、月亮、银河、夜色、星座等夜空相关意象。允许不同措辞、视角和修辞；六行无关散文、指令、代码、重复填充文本或未体现夜空主题的内容不应判为正确。","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_six_nonempty_lines_no_extra_content","normalization":"normalize CRLF/CR to LF; trim only final newline, not arbitrary trailing blank lines","regex":"^[^\\n\\r]+\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\n[^\\n\\r]+$"},{"name":"night_sky_free_verse_semantics","type":"llm_judge","criteria":"Output is a six-line free-verse poem whose central subject is the night sky or clearly associated night-sky imagery. Reject non-poetic prose, meta-commentary, instructions, code, and text unrelated to the night sky. Do not require rhyme, meter, or any particular vocabulary."}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L1.004","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"form":"headline","audience_specificity":"general"},"prompt":"Write a single tweet advertising the grand opening of a new neighborhood bookstore. The entire output must be 280 characters or fewer. Output only the tweet text, with no explanation or label.","ground_truth":{"type":"open_ended_rubric","requirements":["A non-empty, standalone tweet-style promotional message.","Clearly advertises the grand opening, opening celebration, or equivalent launch event of a new bookstore.","Conveys that the bookstore is a neighborhood/community-local bookstore, either explicitly or through an equivalent natural phrasing.","Contains no explanation, analysis, label, or text outside the tweet.","The entire output is 280 Unicode characters or fewer."],"acceptable_variation":"Wording, tone, hashtags, emojis, calls to action, dates, and store names are optional and may vary freely."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"nonempty_and_total_length_le_280","method":"unicode_character_count","min":1,"max":280,"count_entire_output":true},{"name":"no_extraneous_explanation","method":"semantic_rubric","criterion":"Output contains only the intended tweet text and no answer label, explanation, or analysis."},{"name":"bookstore_grand_opening_advertisement","method":"semantic_rubric","criterion":"Output is a promotional message for the grand opening or equivalent launch event of a new neighborhood/community bookstore. Equivalent natural wording is acceptable."}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L1.005","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"general"},"prompt":"Write a four-line rhyming poem about a campfire. Use an AABB rhyme scheme; clear poetic near-rhymes or slant rhymes count when each intended pair is perceptible. Put each line on its own line. Output only the four lines.","ground_truth":{"type":"open_ended_rubric","requirements":["Exactly four nonempty lines.","The poem clearly concerns a campfire or fire at a campsite.","Lines 1 and 2 form one perceptible rhyme or near-rhyme pair, and lines 3 and 4 form another.","Output contains only the four poem lines."],"acceptable_variation":"Near/slant rhymes are accepted when the intended AABB pairing is clear; song/dawn is an explicit acceptable near-rhyme pair in this task."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_four_nonempty_lines","regex":"^[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\s*$"},{"name":"campfire_theme","description":"The four lines must clearly describe, mention, or evoke a campfire, campsite fire, flames, embers, or a fire used in a camping context."},{"name":"aabb_rhyme","description":"The final words or final stressed sounds of lines 1 and 2 must form a perceptible rhyme pair, and lines 3 and 4 must form another. Perfect rhyme is not required. Accept clear near/slant rhymes, explicitly including song/dawn; do not reject solely because the final consonants differ."}],"accepted_examples":["Flames crackle softly in the night,\nThey paint the trees with golden light,\nFriends gather close and share a song,\nWhile glowing embers burn till dawn."],"rejected_examples":["Flames rise beside the lake,\nWe warm our hands by fire,\nThe embers fade at noon,\nWe pack the tent away."],"semantic_judge":"Evaluate the intended sound pairing and campfire meaning, applying the explicit near-rhyme allowance rather than requiring dictionary-perfect rhyme."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if there are not exactly four poem lines, the campfire theme is absent, either intended pair has no perceptible rhyme relationship, or extra commentary appears. Do not fail an expressly allowed near rhyme such as song/dawn."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[],"notes":"Near-rhyme tolerance made explicit after offline review; song/dawn is a passing regression example, while unrelated line endings remain failures."}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"form":"email","audience_specificity":"specific_audience_with_objection"},"prompt":"Write exactly three paragraphs of an email body to your introverted cousin, persuading them to attend your birthday party. The party will have a large crowd. Explicitly acknowledge that a crowd may feel uncomfortable for an introverted person, and offer at least one concrete way you will help them feel more comfortable. Separate each paragraph with exactly one blank line. Include the word “crowd” or “crowded”. Output only the body text: no subject line, greeting, closing, or signature.","ground_truth":{"type":"open_ended","required_content":["Exactly three nonempty paragraphs separated by one blank line","Invites or persuades the cousin to attend the birthday party","Addresses the cousin's introversion and the concern about a large crowd","Offers at least one concrete accommodation, such as arriving early, staying near the host, taking breaks, using a quiet room, or leaving early","Contains “crowd” or “crowded”","Contains no subject line, greeting, closing, signature, or meta-commentary"],"acceptable_variation":"Wording, tone, and the specific accommodation may vary as long as all required content is present."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_check","format_requirements":[{"name":"exactly_three_paragraphs","method":"split_on_blank_lines","expected_count":3,"each_paragraph_nonempty":true},{"name":"mentions_crowd_or_crowded","regex":"(?i)\\b(?:crowd|crowded)\\b"},{"name":"no_subject_greeting_closing_or_signature","method":"heuristic_and_semantic_check"}],"semantic_requirements":["The text persuades or invites the cousin to attend the birthday party.","The text explicitly connects the large crowd to the cousin's introversion, discomfort, or social-energy concern.","The text offers at least one concrete accommodation or plan to reduce that concern."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L2.002","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"form":"blog_post","audience_specificity":"specific_audience_with_objection"},"prompt":"Compose a 4-bullet pitch for adopting AI coding tools, addressed to a senior software engineer who is skeptical of them. Make the case concrete and acknowledge at least one legitimate concern (for example, code quality, security, privacy, or overreliance) with an appropriate safeguard. Each bullet starts with '- ' (dash, space). Output only the four bullets — one per line — and nothing else.","ground_truth":{"type":"rubric","requirements":["Output contains exactly four nonempty dash-space bullets.","All bullets support adopting AI coding tools rather than opposing or discussing an unrelated topic.","The pitch is credibly addressed to a senior software engineer, using engineering-relevant benefits such as tests, refactoring, debugging, documentation, code review, or productivity.","The answer acknowledges at least one plausible skepticism or risk and presents a safeguard or bounded-use practice, such as human review, testing, security controls, privacy controls, or restricted usage.","Bullets should provide substantively distinct points; exact wording is not required."]},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"four_dash_bullets","regex":"^- [^\\n]+\\n- [^\\n]+\\n- [^\\n]+\\n- [^\\n]+\\s*$"},{"name":"semantic_rubric","criteria":["Advocates adoption of AI coding tools.","Targets a skeptical senior software engineer with concrete engineering-relevant reasoning.","Acknowledges at least one legitimate concern and includes a mitigation or safeguard.","Contains four substantially distinct, nontrivial points."],"pass_condition":"all"}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L2.003","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"form":"email","audience_specificity":"specific_audience_with_objection"},"prompt":"Write a polite 3-sentence reply to a customer whose package arrived four days late. Acknowledge the delay, apologize, and offer a reasonable next step or help. Output only the three sentences as a single paragraph with no line breaks. Each sentence must end with a period.","ground_truth":{"acceptance_criteria":["Contains exactly three nonempty sentences in one paragraph, with no line breaks.","Each sentence ends with an English period.","Politely acknowledges that the customer's package was delayed or arrived four days late.","Includes an apology or clear expression of regret.","Offers an appropriate next step, assistance, investigation, or remedy."],"example_answer":"We sincerely apologize that your package arrived four days late. We understand how frustrating this delay must have been and are reviewing what went wrong. Please contact us with your order number so we can help make this right."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_three_period_terminated_sentences_no_linebreaks","regex":"^[^\\r\\n.!?]+\\.[^\\r\\n.!?]+\\.[^\\r\\n.!?]+\\.$"}],"semantic_rubric":["The response is polite and customer-service appropriate.","It acknowledges the late package delivery, preferably including the four-day delay.","It apologizes or expresses regret.","It offers a reasonable next step, assistance, investigation, or remedy."],"pass_condition":"All format requirements pass and all semantic rubric items are satisfied."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"form":"story","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write a persuasive 5-sentence message to a vegetarian friend encouraging them to try a new vegan restaurant. Output exactly one paragraph with no line breaks. End each of the five sentences with an English period. Do not use abbreviations, URLs, or any other periods within a sentence.","ground_truth":"A valid response is exactly one paragraph containing five sentences, each ending with an English period. It addresses a vegetarian friend, encourages them to try a new vegan restaurant, and includes persuasive content such as appealing food, atmosphere, convenience, or an invitation.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"single_paragraph_five_period_terminated_sentences","regex":"^\\s*[^.\\n]+\\.\\s+[^.\\n]+\\.\\s+[^.\\n]+\\.\\s+[^.\\n]+\\.\\s+[^.\\n]+\\.\\s*$"},{"name":"persuasive_vegan_restaurant_message","rubric":"The response must address or clearly target a vegetarian friend, encourage trying a vegan restaurant, and contain at least one persuasive reason or invitation."}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"form":"blog_post","audience_specificity":"specific_audience_with_objection"},"prompt":"Write a 4-paragraph cover letter for a junior data analyst position, addressed to a hiring manager who is skeptical of bootcamp graduates. The letter must mention the word 'bootcamp' explicitly and address that skepticism. Paragraphs separated by a blank line. Output only the body — no header, no signature.","ground_truth":{"required_conditions":["输出恰好四个非空段落，段落之间以至少一个空行分隔。","正文包含不区分大小写的“bootcamp”。","文本为申请 junior data analyst 职位的求职信正文。","文本明确承认并正面回应招聘经理对 bootcamp 毕业生能力或准备程度的怀疑，例如以项目成果、数据技能、实践经历或持续学习作为证据。","不得包含日期、地址、联系方式、主题行、页眉或姓名署名。"],"acceptable_variation":"措辞、称呼方式及用于回应质疑的具体经历可自由变化；无需使用固定模板。"},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_judge","programmatic_checks":[{"name":"mentions_bootcamp","require_case_insensitive_substring":"bootcamp"},{"name":"exactly_four_paragraphs","method":"split_on_blank_lines","require_nonempty_paragraph_count":4},{"name":"no_obvious_header_or_signature","method":"reject_common_header_signature_patterns","patterns":["(?im)^\\s*(date|subject|re:)\\s*:","(?im)^\\s*(dear\\s+[^\\n,]+,?\\s*)$","(?im)^\\s*(sincerely|best regards|kind regards|thank you),?\\s*$"]}],"semantic_rubric":["判定文本是否整体为申请 junior data analyst 职位的求职信正文。","判定文本是否明确回应招聘经理对 bootcamp 毕业生的怀疑，而非仅孤立提到该词。","判定回应是否提供至少一种与数据分析准备度有关的可信证据或论据。","确认没有页眉、地址、联系方式或署名。"],"pass_condition":"全部程序化检查通过，且语义裁判四项均通过。"}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write a limerick in English about a forgetful wizard. It must have exactly five nonempty lines, follow an AABBA rhyme scheme (near rhymes are allowed), and contain no title or commentary. Output only the five lines.","ground_truth":{"acceptance_criteria":["输出恰好五个非空英文行，且没有标题、解释或其他额外文本。","内容明确描写一位健忘的巫师，或其因遗忘造成的情境。","整体具有 limerick 的诗歌形式，前两行与第五行构成 A 韵，第三、四行构成 B 韵；允许自然的近韵和常见重音变体。"],"example_valid_answer":"There once was a wizard named Clare,\nWho misplaced every spell in midair.\nHe forgot where he'd flown,\nThen enchanted a stone,\nAnd rode it back home through the air."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_five_nonempty_lines_no_extra_text","regex":"^[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\r?\\n[^\\n\\r]+\\s*$"},{"name":"semantic_limerick_judgment","instruction":"Judge whether the five lines are an English limerick about a forgetful wizard, with an AABBA rhyme scheme. Accept reasonable near rhymes and natural stress variations. Reject answers that are unrelated to a forgetful wizard, are plainly prose/list text, or do not plausibly have AABBA rhyme."}],"aggregation":"all"}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write an English Shakespearean sonnet about ambition. Use exactly 14 non-empty lines, with the rhyme scheme ABAB CDCD EFEF GG. Each line must be on its own line. Do not include a title, numbering, or any explanation; output only the 14 lines.","ground_truth":{"type":"open_ended_creative","required_properties":["Exactly 14 non-empty output lines","No title, numbering, commentary, or text outside the poem","A coherent English poem whose central theme is ambition","Substantially follows the Shakespearean sonnet rhyme scheme ABAB CDCD EFEF GG"],"acceptable_variation":"Exact meter need not be perfect; near-rhymes may be accepted when the intended rhyme scheme and sonnet structure are clear."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_14_nonempty_lines","method":"split_lines","requirements":{"line_count":14,"each_line_matches":".*\\S.*","allow_single_trailing_newline":true}},{"name":"no_extraneous_text","method":"format_and_content_judge","requirements":["No title","No numbering","No explanatory prose outside the poem"]},{"name":"sonnet_content_and_form","method":"llm_judge","rubric":"Pass only if the text is a coherent English poem centrally about ambition and substantially follows an ABAB CDCD EFEF GG Shakespearean-sonnet rhyme pattern. Allow minor imperfect or near rhymes, but reject unrelated text, prose formatted as lines, and poems lacking a discernible intended rhyme structure."}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write an allegorical poem in which climate change is depicted as a slow-burning fire. Address the poem to general readers. The poem must contain exactly four stanzas of exactly four nonempty lines each, with exactly one blank line between adjacent stanzas. Make the slow-burning-fire metaphor central to the poem. Output only the poem (16 content lines total).","ground_truth":{"type":"rubric","required":["Exactly four stanzas, each containing exactly four nonempty content lines.","Exactly one blank line separates each pair of adjacent stanzas.","The output is a poem only, with no title, explanation, or prefatory text.","The poem substantively depicts climate change through a slow-burning, smoldering, or gradually spreading fire metaphor.","The poem has an allegorical dimension, such as symbolic agents, personification, or a broader implied moral beyond literal description."],"acceptable_variation":"Wording, rhyme, meter, narrative perspective, and the specific allegorical symbols may vary."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_rubric","format_must_satisfy":[{"name":"four_stanzas_four_lines_one_blank_line","regex":"^(?:[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n){3}[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n\\r?\\n(?:[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n){3}[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n\\r?\\n(?:[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n){3}[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n\\r?\\n(?:[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n){3}[^\\r\\n]+\\s*$"}],"semantic_rubric":["Climate change is a substantive subject of the poem.","A slow-burning or smoldering fire is used as the central depiction of climate change.","The poem is allegorical rather than merely a factual statement about climate change."],"decision_rule":"Pass only if the format check passes and all semantic rubric items are judged satisfied."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"form":"poem","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write the first six lines of a villanelle (two tercets) on the theme of loss. Follow the opening villanelle pattern A1 b A2 / a b A1: line 6 must repeat line 1 exactly; lines 1, 3, 4, and 6 must rhyme; lines 2 and 5 must rhyme. Output exactly 6 non-empty lines, formatted as 3 lines, exactly 1 blank line, then 3 lines. Output no title or commentary.","ground_truth":{"format":"Exactly six non-empty poetic lines arranged as two tercets separated by exactly one blank line, with no title or commentary.","villanelle_opening_structure":"A1 b A2 / a b A1; after trimming outer whitespace, line 6 must exactly equal line 1. Lines 1, 3, 4, and 6 should share an end rhyme, and lines 2 and 5 should share a different end rhyme.","content":"The poem must meaningfully evoke loss."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exact_two_tercets","regex":"\\A[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\n[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\n[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\n\\n[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\n[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\n[^\\n\\s](?:[^\\n]*\\S)?\\Z"},{"name":"line_1_repeats_as_line_6","type":"normalized_line_equality","line_a":1,"line_b":6,"normalization":"trim_outer_whitespace"},{"name":"theme_and_rhyme_structure","type":"llm_judge","criteria":["The text is a poem about loss.","Lines 1, 3, 4, and 6 have a perceptibly shared end rhyme.","Lines 2 and 5 have a perceptibly shared end rhyme distinct from the A rhyme."]}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.creative_generation.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.creative_generation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"form":"story","audience_specificity":"specific_audience"},"prompt":"Write a song verse of exactly 8 non-empty lines and a chorus of exactly 4 non-empty lines about missing home. Label the sections exactly as 'Verse:' and 'Chorus:' on their own lines. Put the 8 verse lines immediately after 'Verse:' and the 4 chorus lines immediately after 'Chorus:'. Output only these two labeled sections.","ground_truth":{"type":"open_ended_generation","required_structure":["The complete output begins with a line exactly equal to 'Verse:'.","Exactly 8 non-empty lyric lines follow the Verse label.","The next line is exactly 'Chorus:'.","Exactly 4 non-empty lyric lines follow the Chorus label.","There is no additional text before, between, or after the two sections."],"semantic_requirement":"The lyrics should clearly convey missing home, homesickness, longing for one's hometown, or longing to return home."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_check","format_regex":"\\AVerse:\\r?\\n(?:[^\\r\\n]+\\r?\\n){8}Chorus:\\r?\\n(?:[^\\r\\n]+)(?:\\r?\\n)?\\Z","semantic_rubric":"Pass only if the lyrics clearly express homesickness, longing for home, hometown, family home, or returning home. Do not infer this requirement solely from the presence of the word 'home'."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"far_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"A cook is preparing pasta and boils water in a large pot. Pick the most coherent next sentence: (A) The cook adds salt and dried spaghetti to the pot. (B) The astronaut adjusted the spacecraft's trajectory. (C) The river overflowed its banks. (D) The senator filibustered the bill. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L1.002","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"far_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"A child unwraps a birthday gift. Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The volcano erupted, sending lava down the slope. (B) She squealed with delight at the toy inside. (C) The hedge fund returned 12% last quarter. (D) The submarine descended to 200 meters. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L1.003","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"far_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"A surgeon prepares for an operation. Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The painter mixed cobalt and titanium white. (B) The pirate raised the Jolly Roger. (C) She scrubs her hands and forearms thoroughly. (D) The dragon flew over the mountain. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"C","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"C"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L1.004","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"far_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"A driver pulls into a gas station. Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The librarian stamped the book. (B) The whale breached the surface. (C) The accountant filed the tax return. (D) The driver inserts the nozzle and begins fueling. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"D","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"D"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L1.005","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"far_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"A musician tunes a guitar. Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The geologist examined the rock samples. (B) She plucks each string and adjusts the pegs. (C) The senator filibustered late into the night. (D) The chef seasoned the fish. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"mismatched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'Dear Dr. Smith, I am writing to formally request an extension on the project deadline due to unforeseen circumstances.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) I would greatly appreciate your consideration of a two-week extension. (B) Yo Doc, can u just gimme more time?? (C) The Smith family had three children. (D) I cooked pasta last night. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L2.002","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"mismatched"},"prompt":"Given the opening sentence, \"Once upon a time, in a kingdom far away, there lived a kind queen,\" pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The CPU clock speed exceeded 4 GHz. (B) She ruled with wisdom and was loved by her people. (C) Yo, this queen was kinda mid tho. (D) Insert your debit card to begin. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L2.003","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"same_topic_direct_continuation","register_match":"mismatched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'In this paper, we present a novel approach to graph neural networks.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) Our method achieves state-of-the-art results on three benchmarks. (B) lol it's pretty cool i think. (C) The dragon roared at the knight. (D) BUY NOW! LIMITED TIME! Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"mismatched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'The witness took the stand and was sworn in by the bailiff.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) Press F1 for help (B) the lawyer dude asked some stuff. (C) The cake had three layers. (D) Counsel for the prosecution then began his examination. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"D","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"D"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"mismatched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'A man is teaching a yoga class. He guides students through a sun salutation.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) DUDE THIS POSE IS SICK BRO. (B) He cues each pose in a calm, steady voice. (C) The CFO reported quarterly earnings. (D) Initialize the database connection. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'Maya signed the lease and moved her furniture into the new apartment. The next morning, she met her new neighbor in the hallway.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) Maya introduced herself and learned that her neighbor's name was Ravi. (B) The lease required tenants to pay rent on the first day of every month. (C) The president signed the bill into law. (D) Apples are red. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":[],"notes":"B introduces an unlicensed entity (Tom)."}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'Two friends, Ana and Beto, started a coffee shop in Lima. Within a year, the shop had a loyal local following.' Which continuation best explains the shop's success while maintaining referential continuity, without introducing an unmentioned person or business relationship? (A) Their partner Carlos invested heavily in opening a second location. (B) Ana focused on roasting while Beto handled customer service. (C) The shop was actually in Tokyo. (D) Apples are sweet. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'Dr. Lin arrived at the lab and greeted her postdoc, Sam. She had come to discuss the results of Sam's latest experiment.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) The lab smelled like fresh bread. (B) The grad student, Jordan, was already running the centrifuge. (C) Sam handed Dr. Lin the latest experimental results. (D) Quantum entanglement is weird. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"C","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"C"},"tags":[],"notes":"B introduces unlicensed Jordan."}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"Prefix: \"The detective questioned the suspect in the dimly lit room. Outside, his partner waited.\" Which continuation most directly advances the ongoing interrogation scene? (A) The economy is recovering. (B) The chief inspector planned a vacation abroad. (C) The room had floral wallpaper. (D) After thirty minutes, the suspect finally spoke. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"D","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"D"},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.discourse_coherence.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.discourse_coherence","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"topic_distance":"near_topic_shift","register_match":"matched"},"prompt":"Prefix: 'On the first day of summer camp, Amir met his bunkmate Theo. They shared a single tent at the edge of the woods.' Pick the most coherent continuation: (A) Their counselor, Greg, blew the whistle for dinner. (B) Amir unpacked his sleeping bag while Theo arranged his books. (C) The lake was 50 meters wide. (D) Pizza is delicious. Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":"B directly continues the shared-tent setup; A introduces counselor Greg and shifts to a less directly connected camp event."}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"surface","audience":"novice"},"prompt":"Explain in 2-3 sentences how a thermostat regulates temperature. Your answer must include the words 'sensor' and 'setpoint'. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"A thermostat uses a sensor to measure the current room temperature and compares it with the setpoint. If the temperature differs from the setpoint, it turns the heating or cooling system on or off until the room is near the desired temperature.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric_judge","requirements":["Output contains exactly 2 or 3 sentences.","Output contains the case-insensitive whole words 'sensor' and 'setpoint'.","Explains that the sensor measures or detects the current/environmental temperature.","Explains comparison of the measured temperature with the setpoint.","Explains that the thermostat controls, activates, deactivates, or signals heating and/or cooling in response to the difference."],"disallow":["Meta-commentary, headings, answer labels, or content unrelated to the explanation."],"accept_equivalent_phrasing":true}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L1.002","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"surface","audience":"novice"},"prompt":"Explain in 2-3 sentences what RAM is in a computer. Include the word \"memory\" and convey that the storage is temporary, short-term, or volatile; natural inflections such as \"temporarily\" are accepted. State that RAM is used for data or programs currently in use. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":{"reference":"RAM is a type of memory that stores the data and programs a computer is currently using. It is temporary, so its contents are usually lost when the computer is turned off.","accepted_equivalents":["temporary","temporarily","short-term","volatile","contents are lost when power is removed"],"core_facts":["RAM is computer memory.","It holds data, instructions, or programs currently in use.","Its contents are temporary rather than permanent storage."]},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_explanation_rubric","requirements":["The response is a concise 2-3 sentence explanation, with minor sentence-boundary variation nonbinding when the explanation remains comparably brief.","It identifies RAM as computer memory used to hold data, instructions, or programs currently in use.","It clearly conveys temporary, short-term, or volatile storage. Accept natural morphological and semantic equivalents, including temporarily stores; do not require the exact surface token temporary.","It must not claim RAM is permanent storage or retains its ordinary contents after shutdown."],"accepted_examples":["RAM is a type of computer memory that temporarily stores data and programs currently in use. It allows the computer to access this information quickly while running applications.","RAM is volatile memory for data and instructions a computer is actively using. Its contents are generally lost when power is removed."],"rejected_examples":["RAM is permanent memory that keeps all files after shutdown. Programs use it when they run.","RAM means random access machine."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if the response does not explain RAM, omits its current-use role or temporary/volatile nature, materially contradicts those facts, or consists only of unrelated/meta text. Do not fail solely for temporary versus temporarily."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[],"notes":"Repaired after offline review to preserve non-instr semantic tolerance: temporary, temporarily, short-term, and volatile are equivalent for the core concept."}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L1.003","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"surface","audience":"novice"},"prompt":"Explain in 2-3 sentences how a vaccine works for a beginner. Include the exact word \"immune\" and either \"antibody\" or \"antibodies\". Explain that a vaccine safely trains or prepares the immune system to recognize a germ or part of it, so the body can respond faster in the future. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"A vaccine safely shows the immune system a harmless form or piece of a germ, so it can learn to recognize it. Later, if the real germ enters the body, the immune system can respond faster and make antibodies to help fight it.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite_rubric","requirements":["Output contains exactly 2 or 3 sentences.","Output contains the whole word 'immune'.","Output contains the whole word 'antibody' or 'antibodies'.","Output explains that vaccination safely exposes, trains, or prepares the immune system to recognize a germ, a harmless form of it, a component of it, or genetic instructions for a component.","Output explains that later exposure leads to a faster or more effective immune response, optionally including antibody production or immune memory.","Output does not contain a material medical falsehood, such as claiming that all vaccines give the recipient the disease."],"accept_equivalents":["immune memory","recognize a pathogen","recognize an antigen","weakened or inactivated germ","piece of a germ","mRNA or genetic instructions"]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L1.004","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"surface","audience":"novice"},"prompt":"Explain in 2–3 sentences what photosynthesis is for a novice audience. Include the exact words \"sunlight\" and \"glucose\" (case-insensitive matching is allowed). State that plants, algae, or some bacteria use light energy to make glucose from water and carbon dioxide. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria use sunlight to make glucose from water and carbon dioxide. This process stores energy in glucose and usually releases oxygen.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rule_and_semantic_rubric","requirements":["Output contains exactly 2 or 3 sentences.","Output contains the case-insensitive whole words \"sunlight\" and \"glucose\".","Output identifies photosynthesis as a process used by plants, algae, or some bacteria.","Output states or clearly implies that light energy is used to produce glucose from water and carbon dioxide.","Output contains no substantive scientific contradiction, such as claiming that photosynthesis produces sunlight or converts glucose into carbon dioxide as its main process.","Output contains only the requested explanation and no grading/meta commentary."],"optional_correct_detail":"Mentions oxygen being released."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L1.005","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"surface","audience":"novice"},"prompt":"Explain in 2-3 sentences what a database index is for a beginner. Your answer must include the words 'index' and 'lookup'. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"A database index is an additional data structure that helps a database find relevant rows without scanning every row in a table. It makes a lookup faster, although indexes can use extra storage and may add work when data is changed.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric_judge","requirements":["Output contains exactly 2 or 3 sentences.","Output contains the case-insensitive words 'index' and 'lookup'.","Explains that a database index is an auxiliary data structure or organized reference associated with stored data.","Explains that its purpose is to speed up finding, locating, retrieving, or looking up records/data.","Rejects text that merely contains the required words without a coherent and materially correct explanation."],"allow_equivalents":true}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"operational","audience":"practitioner"},"prompt":"Explain Python list comprehensions in exactly 4-5 sentences. Cover (a) the basic syntax, including an example such as [expression for item in iterable], (b) one common mapping or filtering pattern, and (c) when they are preferable to an explicit for-loop, including a readability caveat. Your answer must include the literal substrings '[' and 'for'. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"A list comprehension creates a new list with syntax such as [expression for item in iterable]. For example, [x * 2 for x in numbers] maps each value in numbers to its double. A common filtering pattern is [x for x in numbers if x > 0], which keeps only positive values. Prefer a list comprehension over an explicit for-loop when building a simple list in one clear expression, but use a for-loop when the logic has multiple steps or becomes hard to read.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric","requirements":[{"name":"sentence_count","criterion":"The response contains 4 or 5 sentences.","required":true},{"name":"required_literals","criterion":"The response contains both literal substrings '[' and 'for'.","required":true},{"name":"basic_syntax","criterion":"Explains that a list comprehension constructs a list using an expression and iteration, with a syntactically recognizable form equivalent to [expression for item in iterable].","required":true},{"name":"common_pattern","criterion":"Provides or accurately describes at least one common mapping or filtering pattern; a filtering pattern should correctly place an optional if condition after the iteration clause.","required":true},{"name":"when_to_prefer","criterion":"States that list comprehensions are suitable for concise, simple list construction and notes that an explicit for-loop is preferable when logic is complex, multi-step, or less readable.","required":true},{"name":"output_scope","criterion":"Contains only the requested explanation, without meta-commentary, headings, or grading discussion.","required":true}],"pass_condition":"All required criteria are satisfied."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L2.002","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"operational","audience":"practitioner"},"prompt":"In 4-5 sentences, explain operationally how to create a Git branch, switch to a branch, and merge a branch into the currently checked-out target branch. Include an example creation command, an example switching command using either `git switch` or `git checkout`, and explain that you switch to the receiving branch before merging. Your answer must include the literal commands `git branch` and `git merge`. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Create a new branch with `git branch feature-login`, which creates the branch from your current commit. Switch to it with `git switch feature-login` and make or commit your changes there. When the work is ready, switch to the branch that should receive the changes, such as `git switch main`. Run `git merge feature-login` while on `main` to merge the feature branch into it.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_rubric","requirements":["Output contains 4 or 5 prose sentences and no material unrelated content.","Explains branch creation and includes the literal substring `git branch` in a command/example context.","Explains switching to a branch and includes either `git switch` or `git checkout` in a command/example context.","Explains merging and includes the literal substring `git merge` in a command/example context.","States or clearly implies that the user checks out/switches to the receiving/target branch before running the merge command."],"pass_threshold":4}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L2.003","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"operational","audience":"practitioner"},"prompt":"Explain how to use a SQL JOIN in exactly 4-5 natural-language sentences. Cover a representative JOIN syntax pattern, the semantic difference between INNER JOIN and LEFT JOIN, and one realistic use case. Your answer must include the exact substrings 'INNER JOIN', 'LEFT JOIN', and ' ON '. Count sentences by terminal punctuation in the prose, and output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"A correct explanation gives a representative SELECT ... FROM ... INNER JOIN ... ON ... pattern, correctly distinguishes matching-row behavior of INNER JOIN from all-left-rows plus NULL right fields for LEFT JOIN, and gives a plausible use case. A separate standalone sentence defining JOIN is not required when the syntax and matching semantics already make the relationship clear.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_explanation_rubric","core_requirements":["Provides or accurately describes representative JOIN syntax involving FROM, a JOIN clause, and ON.","Correctly states that INNER JOIN retains only matching rows from both sides.","Correctly states that LEFT JOIN retains all left-table rows and uses NULL-valued right-side fields when unmatched.","Includes one plausible SQL use case."],"equivalence_policy":"The syntax and matching-row explanation may implicitly establish that JOIN relates rows/tables; do not require a separate definition sentence absent from the task.","presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: 4–5 natural-language sentences, output only the explanation, and include the displayed JOIN substrings."],"reject_if_material_sql_error":true}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a missing core SQL concept or material SQL error; do not invent a separate-definition requirement or fail solely for non-instr presentation differences."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"operational","audience":"practitioner"},"prompt":"In 4-5 sentences, explain how to use Python's `re.search` with a regular-expression pattern. Explain that it searches text for the first match, what it returns when no match is found, and how to use `group()` after a successful search. Your answer must include the lowercase words `pattern`, `match`, and `group`. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Import `re` and call `re.search(pattern, text)` with a regular-expression pattern and the string to search. The function scans the text and returns a match object for the first occurrence, or `None` if nothing matches. Check that the match is not `None` before calling `group()` to obtain the full matched text or a captured group. You can also use methods such as `start()` and `end()` to find the match position.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_rubric","requirements":["Output contains only an explanation and has 4 or 5 sentences.","The lowercase standalone words `pattern`, `match`, and `group` each occur at least once.","Accurately describes calling `re.search` with a regex pattern and text.","Accurately states that `re.search` returns a match object for a successful/first match and `None` when no match is found.","Accurately explains that `group()` is used on a successful match object to retrieve matched text or a capture group."],"reject_if":["Claims that `re.search` returns all matches.","Claims that `group()` may be called on `None` without checking.","Contains only keyword lists, code fragments, or unrelated text rather than an explanation."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"operational","audience":"practitioner"},"prompt":"Explain how to operate a French press coffee maker in 4 or 5 English sentences. Naturally mention the coffee grind or ground coffee, water, and the plunger. Describe the steps in a sensible order, and output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Use coarsely ground coffee in the French press, add hot water, steep it, lower the plunger only after steeping, then pour and serve. Equivalent wording and ordinary inflections such as grind/ground are acceptable.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_explanation_rubric","core_requirements":["Explains operating a French press rather than merely listing vocabulary.","Gives a sensible sequence including coarse grind or ground coffee, hot water, steeping, lowering the plunger, and serving or pouring.","Contains no material operational error such as pressing before steeping or using the plunger to add water."],"semantic_equivalents":{"coffee_preparation":["grind","ground coffee","coarsely ground"],"water":["water","hot water"],"plunger":["plunger","press mechanism"]},"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: 4–5 English sentences and output only the explanation."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a missing core operational step or material operational error; do not fail solely for inflection (for example grind versus ground) or ordinary sentence-count presentation."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"internals_or_design_rationale","audience":"expert"},"prompt":"Explain why TCP uses a three-way handshake (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK) instead of a scheme in which the server considers the connection established immediately after receiving a SYN and sending a SYN-ACK, without waiting for the client's final ACK. In 4-6 sentences, explain (a) the design rationale in terms of confirming both endpoints' initial sequence numbers and communication state, (b) how omitting the final ACK can interact with old or delayed duplicate connection requests and server state, and (c) one trade-off of the three-way design. Use the phrase \"sequence number\" or \"sequence numbers\". Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"TCP's three-way handshake lets each endpoint establish and acknowledge the other's initial sequence number before the server treats the connection as fully established. The final ACK tells the server that the client received the SYN-ACK, so the server has evidence that its reply reached the intended peer rather than merely that a SYN arrived. In a two-message design, an old or delayed duplicate SYN could cause the server to create state for a connection that the client is not actually using, potentially wasting resources or creating an invalid connection. The trade-off is one additional confirmation step and associated startup latency/state handling, in exchange for more robust synchronization and protection against stale connection requests.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric","format_constraints":{"sentence_count":{"min":4,"max":6},"output_only_explanation":true},"required_concepts":[{"id":"mutual_synchronization","description":"Explains that the handshake establishes or confirms both sides' initial sequence numbers and/or that both endpoints can communicate."},{"id":"final_ack_role","description":"Explains that the third ACK confirms to the server that the client received the server's SYN-ACK, or equivalent server-side confirmation."},{"id":"two_way_failure_mode","description":"Identifies a concrete risk of omitting the final ACK, such as old/delayed duplicate SYNs causing spurious server state, half-open/invalid connections, or unnecessary resource allocation."},{"id":"tradeoff","description":"States a trade-off, such as extra setup latency, an additional confirmation step, or temporary state/resource cost."}],"keyword_requirement":{"accept_any":["sequence number","sequence numbers"]},"pass_condition":"All required concepts are present, the keyword requirement is met, and format constraints are satisfied."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"internals_or_design_rationale","audience":"expert"},"prompt":"In 5-7 sentences, explain and compare the design rationale of open addressing and separate chaining for hash-table collision resolution. Discuss how load factor affects expected performance and resizing, compare their memory behavior and cache locality, and mention at least one alternative design (for example Robin Hood hashing, cuckoo hashing, or hopscotch hashing) with a relevant trade-off. Your answer must include the exact words 'collision', 'load factor', and 'cache'. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Hash tables use a hash function to map keys to buckets, but a collision is unavoidable when distinct keys map to the same location. Open addressing keeps entries in the table and probes for another slot, which can improve cache locality and reduce pointer overhead, but performance degrades sharply as the load factor rises and deletion needs care. Separate chaining stores multiple entries per bucket, making insertion and deletion simpler and tolerating a higher load factor, but it uses extra allocations and pointer traversals that are often less cache-friendly. Resizing restores expected constant-time operations in either design, although it incurs occasional rehashing cost. Alternatives such as Robin Hood hashing reduce probe-length variance, while cuckoo hashing offers tightly bounded lookup probes but can require costly relocations or rebuilds during insertion.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_rubric","requirements":[{"id":"format","description":"Output is only an explanation of 5-7 sentences, with no headings, bullet lists, grading commentary, or prompt restatement.","required":true},{"id":"required_terms","description":"Contains the exact lowercase strings 'collision', 'load factor', and 'cache'.","required":true},{"id":"open_addressing","description":"Accurately explains open addressing as resolving collisions by probing/placing entries in table slots and gives at least one relevant trade-off such as clustering, sensitivity to load factor, deletion complexity, or locality.","required":true},{"id":"chaining","description":"Accurately explains separate chaining as storing multiple entries per bucket and gives at least one relevant trade-off such as allocation/pointer overhead, deletion simplicity, high-load behavior, or locality.","required":true},{"id":"comparison","description":"Makes a technically sound comparison involving load factor, resizing, expected performance, memory overhead, or cache locality.","required":true},{"id":"alternative","description":"Mentions at least one legitimate alternative collision-resolution design and a plausible associated trade-off.","required":true}],"pass_condition":"All required requirements are satisfied. Accept equivalent technically correct terminology, including 'separate chaining', 'closed hashing' for open addressing where unambiguous, and valid alternatives such as cuckoo, Robin Hood, hopscotch, or Swiss-table-style control metadata. Reject answers with materially false claims, such as asserting that chaining eliminates collisions or that open addressing remains unaffected by load factor."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"internals_or_design_rationale","audience":"expert"},"prompt":"In 4-6 sentences, explain why React historically used a virtual-DOM-based reconciliation approach for declarative UI updates. Compare it with imperative direct DOM manipulation and compile-time approaches such as Svelte's, including at least one advantage and one cost or limitation of each model. Do not claim that a virtual DOM is inherently faster in all cases. Your answer must include the exact words 'reconciliation' and 'DOM'. Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"React historically used a virtual DOM to let developers describe UI as a function of state while React performs reconciliation to determine the required DOM updates. This separates application code from imperative mutation bookkeeping and enables predictable composition, batching, and reuse of the rendering model across targets. Direct DOM manipulation can be efficient for small, localized updates, but application code must manually preserve consistency as state and UI complexity grow. Compile-time systems such as Svelte can often generate narrower update code by analyzing dependencies ahead of time, avoiding some runtime virtual-tree work. The trade-off is that virtual-DOM reconciliation adds allocation and comparison overhead and is not inherently faster, whereas compile-time approaches depend more on what can be determined during compilation and may offer different runtime flexibility.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric_plus_format","format_checks":{"sentence_count":{"min":4,"max":6},"required_case_insensitive_terms":["reconciliation","DOM"],"output_only_explanation":true},"rubric":[{"criterion":"Explains that React's virtual-DOM approach supports declarative, state-driven UI updates and reconciliation rather than presenting it merely as universally faster.","required":true},{"criterion":"Addresses direct imperative DOM manipulation and gives a meaningful trade-off, such as manual consistency/bookkeeping versus localized control or efficiency.","required":true},{"criterion":"Addresses a compile-time approach such as Svelte and gives a meaningful trade-off, such as less runtime diffing via generated updates versus reliance on compile-time analysis or different flexibility constraints.","required":true},{"criterion":"States at least one cost or limitation of virtual-DOM reconciliation, such as runtime comparison, allocation, memory, or non-universal performance benefits.","required":true}],"pass_condition":"All format checks pass and all required rubric criteria are substantively satisfied. Accept technically equivalent wording; do not require the reference answer's exact phrasing."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"internals_or_design_rationale","audience":"expert"},"prompt":"Explain why many modern high-performance CPUs use out-of-order execution. In 4–6 sentences, explain how it improves use of the pipeline when an instruction is stalled on a dependency, contrast it with in-order execution, and state one concrete trade-off. Mention at least one relevant implementation mechanism, such as register renaming, dynamic scheduling, a reservation station, or a reorder buffer. Your answer must include the exact words \"pipeline\" and \"dependency\". Output only the explanation.","ground_truth":"Out-of-order execution lets a CPU issue later independent instructions while an earlier instruction waits for a long-latency operation or an unresolved dependency, improving instruction-level parallelism and keeping the pipeline busy. An in-order CPU generally issues instructions in program order, so a stall near the front can prevent later ready instructions from executing. Dynamic scheduling, often aided by register renaming and structures such as reservation stations or a reorder buffer, finds ready work while preserving the appearance of architectural program order at retirement. The trade-off is substantially greater hardware complexity, area, power consumption, and verification burden, especially for speculation and precise recovery from exceptions or mispredictions. Simpler or power-constrained processors may therefore use in-order execution instead.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric_semantic_and_format","requirements":["Contains the exact words \"pipeline\" and \"dependency\".","Contains 4 to 6 sentences and no material outside the explanation.","Correctly states that out-of-order execution can execute or issue later independent ready instructions while earlier instructions wait, thereby improving utilization or instruction-level parallelism.","Correctly contrasts in-order execution as constrained by program-order issue/execution such that stalls can block subsequent instructions.","States at least one concrete trade-off, such as greater hardware complexity, power, area, verification difficulty, speculation/recovery complexity, or potentially less predictable timing.","Mentions at least one relevant implementation mechanism: register renaming, dynamic scheduling, reservation station, reorder buffer, or equivalent."],"reject_conditions":["Claims that out-of-order execution violates architectural program order without qualification.","Claims that all modern CPUs use out-of-order execution.","Omits any required semantic component despite containing the required keywords."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.expository_explanation.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.expository_explanation","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"concept_depth":"internals_or_design_rationale","audience":"expert"},"prompt":"Explain why JWTs are commonly used as signed JWSs rather than encrypted JWEs. Distinguish integrity/authenticity from confidentiality, explain that a signed JWT's claims are generally readable, and compare this design with server-side sessions identified by cookies and with encrypted JWTs. Discuss concrete trade-offs, including scalability, revocation, key management, performance, and confidentiality. Your answer must include the words 'signature' and 'stateless'. Output only the explanation, in 4-6 sentences.","ground_truth":"A JWT is commonly signed because a signature lets a recipient verify integrity and issuer authenticity without requiring the recipient to contact a central session store. This supports stateless verification and can simplify scaling across services, but the claims in an ordinary signed JWS are encoded rather than confidential and should not contain secrets. A server-side session carried by an opaque cookie can make revocation and server-side session control easier, at the cost of session storage, replication, or lookup infrastructure. An encrypted JWT (JWE) can protect claim confidentiality, but adds encryption-key management, processing overhead, and operational/interoperability complexity. Thus signing is often sufficient when claims need to be tamper-evident rather than secret, while encryption or server-side sessions are preferable when confidentiality or immediate revocation is important.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"rubric","format_requirements":{"sentence_count":{"min":4,"max":6},"required_substrings":["signature","stateless"],"output_only_explanation":true},"criteria":[{"id":"signed_not_encrypted","requirement":"Explains that signing provides integrity and/or issuer authenticity, not confidentiality, and that ordinary signed JWT claims are readable/decodable.","weight":3},{"id":"stateless_tradeoff","requirement":"Explains stateless/distributed verification or scalability and at least one associated limitation such as revocation, token theft, or stale claims.","weight":2},{"id":"server_session_alternative","requirement":"Compares JWTs with a server-side session represented by an opaque cookie/session ID, including a state-storage or revocation trade-off.","weight":2},{"id":"encrypted_token_alternative","requirement":"Explains that JWE/encrypted tokens provide confidentiality and identifies at least one cost such as key management, overhead, or complexity.","weight":2},{"id":"balanced_conclusion","requirement":"Presents signing, encryption, and server-side sessions as context-dependent choices rather than claiming JWTs can never be encrypted.","weight":1}],"pass_threshold":8,"critical_failures":["Claims that a signature encrypts or hides JWT claims.","Claims that JWTs cannot be encrypted."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"script":"cyrillic","constraint_class":"counting"},"prompt":"Напишите ровно 3 предложения о пользе чтения. Используйте только русский язык и кириллицу. Не используйте латинские буквы. Каждое предложение должно заканчиваться точкой, восклицательным или вопросительным знаком; не используйте сокращения и многоточия.","ground_truth":"Ровно 3 непустых русских предложения о пользе чтения. Каждое предложение содержит кириллические русские буквы и заканчивается одним из знаков: . ! ?. Латинские буквы и иные письменности не допускаются.","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_russian_cyrillic_and_punctuation","regex":"(?s)^[А-Яа-яЁё\\s,;:—–«»„“”()\\-]+[.!?](?:\\s+[А-Яа-яЁё\\s,;:—–«»„“”()\\-]+[.!?]){2}\\s*$"},{"name":"three_nonempty_cyrillic_sentences","regex":"(?s)^(?=(?:[^.!?]*[А-Яа-яЁё][^.!?]*[.!?]\\s*){3}$)[А-Яа-яЁё\\s,;:—–«»„“”()\\-]+[.!?](?:\\s+[А-Яа-яЁё\\s,;:—–«»„“”()\\-]+[.!?]){2}\\s*$"}]},"tags":["language:ru"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L1.002","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"script":"cyrillic","constraint_class":"counting"},"prompt":"Напишите ровно 5 непустых предложений на русском языке об осени. В каждом предложении должен быть хотя бы один русский словесный фрагмент. Не используйте латинские буквы (A–Z, a–z). Используйте обычные знаки конца предложения: «.», «!» или «?».","ground_truth":{"type":"constraint_based","requirements":["Ровно 5 непустых предложений.","Текст написан преимущественно по-русски и содержит кириллицу.","Тема текста — осень.","В тексте отсутствуют латинские буквы A–Z и a–z."],"example_valid_answer":"Осень принесла прохладные дни. Листья на деревьях стали золотыми. В парке тихо шуршит листва. Часто идёт мелкий дождь. Я люблю гулять в осеннем лесу."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_constraint_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"no_latin_letters","regex":"^[^A-Za-z]*$"},{"name":"contains_cyrillic","regex":"[А-Яа-яЁё]"},{"name":"five_nonempty_sentences","method":"normalize whitespace; split on one or more terminal characters [.!?]+; discard trailing empty segment only; require exactly 5 remaining segments, each containing at least one Cyrillic letter"},{"name":"autumn_topic","regex":"(?i)\\b(осень|осенью|осен[а-яё]*)\\b"}],"notes":"如需支持更广泛的拉丁字符，应使用 Unicode Script=Latin 检测。主题判定采用关键词会漏掉无“осен-”词根但语义正确的回答；若基准允许语义评审，应以语义分类器或人工判定替代该硬正则。"}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:ru"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L1.003","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"script":"cyrillic","constraint_class":"counting"},"prompt":"Опишите море ровно в 2 предложениях на русском языке. Используйте русские буквы кириллицы; пробелы и русские знаки препинания разрешены. Не используйте латинские буквы, цифры или другие письменности.","ground_truth":"Принимается ответ, который: (1) содержит ровно два предложения, завершённые знаками . ! или ?; (2) написан по-русски и описывает море; (3) содержит кириллические буквы в каждом предложении; (4) не содержит латинских букв, цифр или букв иных письменностей; (5) использует только кириллические буквы, пробелы/переводы строк и допустимую русскую пунктуацию.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_language_semantic_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_characters","regex":"^[А-Яа-яЁё\\s.,!?;:«»—-]+$"},{"name":"two_sentences","regex":"(?s)^\\s*[^.!?]+[.!?]\\s+[^.!?]+[.!?]\\s*$"},{"name":"cyrillic_in_each_sentence","regex":"(?s)^\\s*[^.!?]*[А-Яа-яЁё][^.!?]*[.!?]\\s+[^.!?]*[А-Яа-яЁё][^.!?]*[.!?]\\s*$"}],"additional_checks":["Russian language identification for the full response","Semantic check that the response describes the sea"]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:ru"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L1.004","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"script":"cyrillic","constraint_class":"counting"},"prompt":"Напишите ровно 4 предложения на русском о пользе спорта. Все буквы должны быть русскими кириллическими буквами; разрешены пробелы, переводы строк и только знаки конца предложения: . ! ?. Каждое предложение должно заканчиваться одним из этих знаков.","ground_truth":"Ответ должен содержать ровно 4 русских предложения о пользе спорта. Каждое предложение должно содержать хотя бы одну русскую кириллическую букву и оканчиваться на . ! или ?. Допустимы только русские кириллические буквы А-Я, а-я, Ё, ё, пробелы, переводы строк и знаки . ! ?. Пример: «Спорт укрепляет здоровье. Регулярные тренировки развивают выносливость. Движение улучшает настроение. Командные игры учат сотрудничеству.»","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"hybrid_format_and_semantic_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_characters","regex":"(?s)^[А-Яа-яЁё\\s.!?]+$"},{"name":"four_nonempty_sentences","regex":"(?s)^\\s*[А-Яа-яЁё\\s]+[.!?]\\s+[А-Яа-яЁё\\s]+[.!?]\\s+[А-Яа-яЁё\\s]+[.!?]\\s+[А-Яа-яЁё\\s]+[.!?]\\s*$"}],"semantic_rubric":"确认四个句子均为俄语，整体内容说明体育或运动的益处；不得仅重复无意义字符或无关文本。"}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:ru"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L1.005","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"script":"cyrillic","constraint_class":"counting"},"prompt":"Напишите ровно три предложения на русском языке о вашем любимом или выбранном времени года. Используйте только русские кириллические буквы, пробелы и знаки препинания «.», «!», «?». Не используйте латиницу, цифры или другие письменности.","ground_truth":"Принимается любой ответ, который содержит ровно три непустых предложения на русском языке о любимом или выбранном времени года; каждое предложение заканчивается одним из знаков . ! ?; весь ответ содержит только русские кириллические буквы (включая Ё/ё), пробелы и знаки . ! ?; латиница, цифры и иные письменности отсутствуют.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["After trimming outer whitespace, the response contains exactly three nonempty sentences; each sentence ends with exactly one of '.', '!', or '?'.","Every non-whitespace, non-sentence-terminal character is a Russian Cyrillic letter in А-Я, а-я, Ё, or ё; Latin letters, digits, emoji, and other scripts are absent.","The text is grammatical Russian, and the three sentences collectively describe a favorite or selected season."],"fail_criteria":["The response has other than three sentences, contains a forbidden character or script, is not Russian, or is not about a favorite or selected season."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:ru"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"script":"devanagari","constraint_class":"marker_placement"},"prompt":"हिंदी में ठीक 5 वाक्य लिखें। हर वाक्य का अंत “।” से करें। कम से कम दो अलग-अलग अंशों को *इस तरह* Markdown तारांक से हाइलाइट करें। पाठ में ठीक एक बार [नाम] लिखें। तारांक (*), वर्ग कोष्ठक ([ और ]) और रिक्त स्थान के अतिरिक्त, सभी अक्षर देवनागरी में हों। कोई शीर्षक, सूची, व्याख्या या अतिरिक्त पाठ न दें।","ground_truth":"आज [नाम] विद्यालय गया। उसने *नई पुस्तक* पढ़ी। शिक्षक ने *अच्छा काम* कहा। फिर सभी बच्चे मैदान में खेले। शाम को वह घर लौट आया।","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exact_placeholder_once","regex":"^(?=[\\s\\S]*\\[नाम\\])(?!(?:[\\s\\S]*\\[नाम\\]){2})[\\s\\S]*$"},{"name":"five_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^।]*।){5}$"},{"name":"at_least_two_highlights","regex":"\\*[^*\\n]+\\*[\\s\\S]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*"},{"name":"allowed_characters_only","regex":"^[\\u0900-\\u097F\\s*\\[\\]।,!?]+$"}]},"tags":["language:hi"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L2.002","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"script":"devanagari","constraint_class":"marker_placement"},"prompt":"हिंदी में ठीक 6 वाक्य लिखें। प्रत्येक वाक्य का अंत देवनागरी पूर्णविराम “।” से करें। ठीक 3 गैर-रिक्त अंशों को Markdown के *इस तरह* हाइलाइट करें। ठीक एक बार [स्थान] शामिल करें। *, [, ], रिक्त स्थान और “।” को छोड़कर, केवल देवनागरी वर्णों का उपयोग करें।","ground_truth":{"constraints":{"sentence_count":6,"sentence_terminator":"।","exact_highlight_count":3,"highlight_nonempty":true,"required_literal_placeholder":"[स्थान]","placeholder_count":1,"allowed_non_devanagari_characters":["*","[","]"," ","।","\n"]},"example_answer":"*राम* [स्थान] में रहता है। वह हर सुबह विद्यालय जाता है। *उसकी बहन* पुस्तक पढ़ती है। आज मौसम बहुत सुहावना है। वे शाम को *बगीचे* में खेलते हैं। फिर सब घर लौट आते हैं।"},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"composite_format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_characters_only","regex":"^[\\u0900-\\u097F*\\[\\] \\n]+$"},{"name":"exactly_six_sentences","count_literal":{"literal":"।","equals":6}},{"name":"required_placeholder_once","count_literal":{"literal":"[स्थान]","equals":1}},{"name":"exactly_three_highlights","regex":"^(?:[^*]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){3}[^*]*$"}]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:hi"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L2.003","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"script":"devanagari","constraint_class":"marker_placement"},"prompt":"हिंदी में चाय के बारे में ठीक 4 वाक्य लिखें। हर वाक्य का अंत “।” से करें। दो अलग-अलग खंडों को Markdown के *तारांकित चिह्नों* से highlight करें और ठीक एक [प्लेसहोल्डर] रखें। *, [, ], और रिक्त स्थान के अलावा केवल देवनागरी वर्णों का उपयोग करें।","ground_truth":"चाय एक लोकप्रिय पेय है। *गरम चाय* सुबह अच्छी लगती है। [स्वाद] के लिए लोग इसमें मसाले डालते हैं। *हरी चाय* भी स्वास्थ्य के लिए उपयोगी है।","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_characters_only","regex":"^[\\u0900-\\u097F\\s*\\[\\]]+$"},{"name":"exactly_four_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^।]*।){4}$"},{"name":"exactly_two_highlights","regex":"^(?:[^*]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){2}[^*]*$"},{"name":"exactly_one_placeholder","regex":"^(?:[^\\[]*\\[[^\\]\\n]+\\]){1}[^\\[]*$"},{"name":"highlight_contents_devanagari","regex":"^(?:[^*]*\\*[\\u0900-\\u097F\\s]+\\*){2}[^*]*$"},{"name":"placeholder_contents_devanagari","regex":"^(?:[^\\[]*\\[[\\u0900-\\u097F\\s]+\\]){1}[^\\[]*$"},{"name":"topic_tea","regex":"(?:चाय|चहा)"}]},"tags":["language:hi"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"script":"devanagari","constraint_class":"marker_placement"},"prompt":"हिंदी में ठीक 5 वाक्य लिखें। हर वाक्य का अंत “।” से करें। कम से कम 2 अलग-अलग गैर-खाली अंशों को *इस प्रकार* चिह्नित करें और कम से कम 1 गैर-खाली [स्थानधारक] शामिल करें। *, [, ], रिक्त स्थान और “।” के अतिरिक्त, केवल देवनागरी वर्णों का उपयोग करें।","ground_truth":"*सुंदर बगीचा* सुबह खुला। बच्चे वहाँ खेलते हैं। [स्थानधारक] आज आएगा। *ठंडी हवा* सबको अच्छी लगी। हम शाम को घर लौटे।","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"exactly_five_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^।]*।){5}$"},{"name":"two_highlights","regex":"(?s)^(?=(?:.*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){2}).*$"},{"name":"placeholder_with_devanagari_content","regex":"\\[[\\u0900-\\u097f ]+\\]"},{"name":"allowed_characters_only","regex":"^[\\u0900-\\u097f *\\[\\]।\\n]+$"}]},"tags":["language:hi"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"script":"devanagari","constraint_class":"marker_placement"},"prompt":"देवनागरी में किसी भारतीय त्योहार के बारे में ठीक 4 वाक्य लिखें। ठीक दो अलग-अलग गैर-रिक्त अंशों को *...* में लिखें और ठीक एक गैर-रिक्त स्थानधारक को [... ] में लिखें। पाठ और स्थानधारक के भीतर केवल देवनागरी वर्णों का उपयोग करें; *, [, ], रिक्त स्थान और वाक्य-समाप्ति चिह्न । केवल प्रारूप के लिए अनुमत हैं।","ground_truth":"दीवाली भारत का प्रसिद्ध त्योहार है। लोग *दीप जलाते हैं* और घर सजाते हैं। बच्चे [मिठाई] बाँटते हैं। यह पर्व *खुशी और एकता* का संदेश देता है।","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"custom_validator","requirements":["回答按天城文句号“。”分割后必须恰好有4个非空句子，且不得含额外非空文本。","全文必须恰好有2个不嵌套、非空的 *...* 片段。","全文必须恰好有1个非空的 [...] 片段，且方括号内只含天城文字符和空白。","除 *、[、]、空白和天城文句号“。”外，去除格式标记后的所有字符必须属于天城文 Unicode 区间 U+0900–U+097F。","去除格式标记后必须是关于印度节日的印地语文本；若不具备可靠语义分类能力，应改为要求并检查至少出现一个指定天城文节日名称，例如 दीवाली、होली、ईद、पोंगल、ओणम。"]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:hi"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"script":"hanzi","constraint_class":"punctuation"},"prompt":"请用中文写恰好3句话介绍北京。每句话必须以中文句号“。”结尾。不要使用任何逗号，包括中文逗号“，”和英文逗号“,”。请用星号将至少两段非空文字高亮，例如“*北京*”。除高亮星号“*”和句末中文句号“。”外，只能使用汉字；不得使用空格、数字、拉丁字母或其他标点。","ground_truth":"*北京*是中国的首都。*故宫*展现悠久历史。北京拥有丰富文化。","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"allowed_characters","regex":"^(?:[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]+|\\*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]+\\*|。)+$"},{"name":"exactly_three_sentences","regex":"^(?:[\\u4e00-\\u9fff*]+。){3}$"},{"name":"no_commas","regex":"(?s)^[^,，]*$"},{"name":"two_highlights","regex":"^(?=(?:[^*]*\\*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]+\\*){2})(?:[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]+|\\*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]+\\*|。)+$"}]},"tags":["language:zh"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"script":"hanzi","constraint_class":"punctuation"},"prompt":"请用中文写恰好4个完整句子谈谈学习的重要性。每个句子必须以中文句号“。”结束。禁止使用任何逗号（中文“，”与英文“,”均不可）。恰好使用3对星号高亮3处文本，且不得使用其他星号。","ground_truth":"学习能帮助我们理解世界。它让我们获得*知识*并培养*能力*。持续学习可以提升解决问题的*信心*。因此我们应当珍惜每一次学习机会。","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["The response is principally grammatical Chinese and materially discusses the importance of learning.","It contains exactly four complete nonempty sentences and every sentence ends with the Chinese full stop '。'.","It contains neither a Chinese comma '，' nor an ASCII comma ','.","Exactly three nonempty spans are highlighted with three pairs of single asterisks, and no other asterisks occur."],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a non-Chinese or off-topic response, a sentence-count/terminator violation, any comma, or an invalid number/placement of asterisks."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:zh"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"script":"hanzi","constraint_class":"punctuation"},"prompt":"请用中文写一段介绍春节的话。必须恰好包含5个句子，且每个句子都以中文句号“。”结尾。不允许使用任何逗号，包括“，”和“,”。请恰好使用两组 *...* 突出显示两处内容，除此之外不得使用星号。","ground_truth":"春节是中国重要的传统节日。人们常在节前打扫房屋并准备年货。除夕夜家人会一起吃*年夜饭*。许多地方还有贴春联和燃放烟花的习俗。人们也会互相送上*新年祝福*。","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"no_commas","regex":"(?s)^[^,，]*$"},{"name":"exactly_five_period_terminated_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^。\\n]+。\\s*){5}$"},{"name":"exactly_two_highlights_and_no_extra_asterisks","regex":"^(?:[^*]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){2}[^*]*$"},{"name":"contains_hanzi","regex":"[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]"},{"name":"topic_spring_festival","regex":"(?:春节|新春|农历新年|过年|新年)"}]},"tags":["language:zh"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"script":"hanzi","constraint_class":"punctuation"},"prompt":"用中文回答。恰好写3个以“。”结尾的句子来说明什么是友谊。不要使用任何逗号（“，”或“,”均不可）。恰好使用两对星号，以 *...* 形式高亮两段非空文本，除此之外不要使用星号。","ground_truth":"示例合规答案：友谊是彼此信任和支持的关系。真正的朋友会在困难时给予*帮助*。这份陪伴能带来*温暖*。","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"no_commas","regex":"(?s)^[^,，]*$"},{"name":"exactly_three_chinese_full_stop_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^。\\n]*。\\s*){3}$"},{"name":"exactly_two_nonempty_highlights","regex":"(?s)^(?:[^*]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){2}[^*]*$"},{"name":"contains_hanzi","regex":"[\\u4e00-\\u9fff]"},{"name":"topic_friendship","regex":"(?:友谊|友情|朋友|挚友|友爱)"}]},"tags":["language:zh"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.non_latin_script_robustness","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"script":"hanzi","constraint_class":"punctuation"},"prompt":"请用中文写3句话介绍长城。每句话都必须以“。”结尾。禁止使用任何逗号（中文“，”与英文“,”均不可）。用 *...* 至少高亮2个短语。","ground_truth":"*长城*是中国古代规模宏大的防御工程。它横跨多个地区并承载着丰富的历史文化。*八达岭长城*是著名的参观地点。","scorer":{"type":"format_check","must_satisfy":[{"name":"no_commas","regex":"(?s)^[^,，]*$"},{"name":"exactly_three_period_terminated_sentences","regex":"^(?:[^。\\n]*。\\s*){3}$"},{"name":"two_highlights","regex":"(?s)^(?:[^*]*\\*[^*\\n]+\\*){2,}[^*]*$"},{"name":"hanzi_in_each_sentence","regex":"^(?=[^。]*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff][^。]*。)(?=[^。]*。[^。]*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff][^。]*。)(?=[^。]*。[^。]*。[^。]*[\\u4e00-\\u9fff][^。]*。)[\\s\\S]*$"},{"name":"topic_great_wall","regex":"(?:长城|八达岭(?:关|长城)?|居庸关|山海关|嘉峪关)"}]},"tags":["language:zh"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.ordinal_indexing.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.ordinal_indexing","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"reference":"absolute_end","sequence_kind":"explicit_list"},"prompt":"Sequence (left to right): red, blue, green, yellow, purple, orange. What is the third item from the right? Reply with one word.","ground_truth":"yellow","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yellow","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true,"allow_terminal_punctuation":true},"tags":[],"notes":""}
