{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"register_variant"},"prompt":"Read: 'Ana always deliberately says things she knows are false, while Bo always tells lies.' In this sentence, are 'deliberately says things she knows are false' and 'tells lies' near-synonyms? Reply with exactly one of: opposites / synonyms.","ground_truth":"synonyms","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"synonyms","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[]}
