{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"deliberately_obscured"},"prompt":"In a logic-puzzle setup, Amy is described as 'always speaking mistruths' and Sam as 'always lying.' Considering only whether the statements they make are true or false, are Amy and Sam the same type of character? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no.","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"deliberately_obscured"},"prompt":"Assume that both descriptions concern only declarative claims made by the NPC, and that a claim is either true or false. Do “Olga always makes false claims” and “Pavel never makes a true claim” describe the same NPC type? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no.","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"deliberately_obscured"},"prompt":"For this question, define a “fabrication” as any untrue statement, regardless of whether it was intentional. In a story, Mateo states only fabrications and Nell speaks only untruths. Under this definition, are their speech behaviors equivalent? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no.","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"deliberately_obscured"},"prompt":"Aria is described as a witness whose every factual assertion is false. Bashir is described in exactly the same way: every factual assertion he makes is false. Under these stipulated descriptions, are Aria and Bashir behaviorally equivalent with respect to truthfulness? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no.","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.semantic_precision.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.semantic_precision","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"synonymy_distance":"deliberately_obscured"},"prompt":"Assume every robot output is a declarative statement with exactly one of two truth values: true or false. R1 outputs only false statements, and R2 outputs no true statements. Are R1 and R2 behaviorally identical with respect to truth-telling? Reply with exactly one of: yes / no.","ground_truth":"yes","scorer":{"type":"exact_match_string","expected":"yes","case_sensitive":false,"strip_whitespace":true},"tags":[]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L1.001","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following English sentence to Spanish: 'The library opens at nine in the morning.' Output only the Spanish translation, nothing else.","ground_truth":["La biblioteca abre a las nueve de la mañana.","La biblioteca abre a las nueve de la mañana"],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:La\\ biblioteca\\ abre\\ a\\ las\\ nueve\\ de\\ la\\ mañana|La\\ biblioteca\\ abre\\ a\\ las\\ nueve\\ de\\ la\\ mañana)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->es"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L1.002","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate to French: 'I would like a cup of coffee, please.' Output only the French translation.","ground_truth":["Je voudrais une tasse de café, s'il vous plaît.","Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît.","J'aimerais une tasse de café, s'il vous plaît.","J'aimerais un café, s'il vous plaît."],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:Je voudrais une tasse de café, s['’]il vous plaît|Je voudrais un café, s['’]il vous plaît|J['’]aimerais une tasse de café, s['’]il vous plaît|J['’]aimerais un café, s['’]il vous plaît)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->fr"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L1.003","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate to German: 'Where is the train station?' Output only the German translation.","ground_truth":["Wo ist der Bahnhof?","Wo befindet sich der Bahnhof?"],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:Wo\\ ist\\ der\\ Bahnhof|Wo\\ befindet\\ sich\\ der\\ Bahnhof)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->de"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L1.004","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate to Italian: 'My favorite color is blue.' Output only the Italian translation.","ground_truth":["Il mio colore preferito è il blu.","Il mio colore preferito è blu."],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:Il\\ mio\\ colore\\ preferito\\ è\\ il\\ blu|Il\\ mio\\ colore\\ preferito\\ è\\ blu)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->it"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L1.005","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L1","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate to Portuguese: 'Tomorrow we will travel to Lisbon.' Output only the Portuguese translation.","ground_truth":["Amanhã viajaremos para Lisboa.","Amanhã vamos viajar para Lisboa.","Amanhã iremos viajar para Lisboa."],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:Amanhã\\ viajaremos\\ para\\ Lisboa|Amanhã\\ vamos\\ viajar\\ para\\ Lisboa|Amanhã\\ iremos\\ viajar\\ para\\ Lisboa)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->pt"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L2.001","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"slang_or_idiom"},"prompt":"Translate the English idiom 'It's raining cats and dogs.' into French as a natural French idiomatic equivalent (do NOT translate literally). Output only the French translation.","ground_truth":{"accepted_examples":["Il pleut des cordes.","Il tombe des cordes.","Il pleut à verse."],"evaluation_note":"Accept other natural French idiomatic or conventional expressions meaning that it is raining very heavily; reject literal translations involving cats/chats and dogs/chiens."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"llm_judge","rubric":"Pass only if the response contains only a French translation and conveys the idiomatic meaning of very heavy rain using a natural French idiom or conventional expression. Accept, for example, “Il pleut des cordes”, “Il tombe des cordes”, and “Il pleut à verse”. Reject literal translations mentioning cats/chats or dogs/chiens, unrelated French sentences, answers that merely contain pleut/tombe without the intended meaning, and responses with explanatory text."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:en->fr","idiom"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L2.002","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"slang_or_idiom"},"prompt":"In Spanish theatrical usage, translate the English good-luck idiom “Break a leg!” using its natural non-literal equivalent. Output only the Spanish expression.","ground_truth":"¡Mucha mierda!","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*¡?\\s*mucha\\s+mierda\\s*!?\\s*$","flags":["i"]},"tags":["language:en->es","idiom"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L2.003","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"slang_or_idiom"},"prompt":"Translate the French idiom “avoir le coup de foudre” into a concise, natural English equivalent. Do not translate it literally. Output only the translation.","ground_truth":["love at first sight","fall in love at first sight"],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:love at first sight|(?:to )?fall in love at first sight)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:fr->en","idiom"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"slang_or_idiom"},"prompt":"Translate the English idiom \"spilling the beans\" (meaning revealing a secret) into a natural Spanish idiom, not a literal translation. Output only one Spanish phrase.","ground_truth":["irse de la lengua","descubrir el pastel"],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:irse\\ de\\ la\\ lengua|descubrir\\ el\\ pastel)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->es","idiom"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_high","register":"slang_or_idiom"},"prompt":"Translate the German idiom 'Tomaten auf den Augen haben' into a natural English idiom or phrase that conveys the same meaning. Output only the English translation.","ground_truth":"to be blind to the obvious","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*(?:(?:to )?be blind to (?:the )?obvious|(?:to )?be oblivious to (?:the )?obvious|(?:to )?not notice (?:the )?obvious|(?:to )?not see what(?:'s| is) right in front of (?:one['’]s|your|his|her|their) (?:eyes|nose)|(?:to )?miss what(?:'s| is) right in front of (?:one['’]s|your|his|her|their) (?:eyes|nose)|(?:to )?have (?:one['’]s|your|his|her|their) eyes closed)\\s*[.!]?\\s*$","flags":["i"]},"tags":["language:de->en","idiom"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_low","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following passage to Swahili: 'In the early morning the village awoke to the sound of birds singing in the acacia trees. The children helped their parents fetch water from the well, while the elders gathered under the great baobab to discuss the day's plans.' Output only the Swahili translation.","ground_truth":"Mapema asubuhi, kijiji kiliamka kwa sauti ya ndege waliokuwa wakiimba kwenye miti ya migunga. Watoto waliwasaidia wazazi wao kuchota maji kutoka kisimani, huku wazee wakikusanyika chini ya mbuyu mkubwa kujadili mipango ya siku hiyo.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_rubric","language":"sw","output_constraints":["Output must consist only of a Swahili translation, with no explanation or English source passage.","Minor orthographic, lexical, tense, and syntactic variation is acceptable."],"criteria":[{"id":"scene","requirement":"Conveys that early in the morning the village awoke because of/to the sound of birds singing in acacia trees.","weight":0.4},{"id":"water","requirement":"Conveys that the children helped their parents fetch/draw water from a well.","weight":0.3},{"id":"plans","requirement":"Conveys that the elders gathered under a large/great baobab tree to discuss the day's plans.","weight":0.3}],"pass_condition":"All three criteria must be substantially satisfied; allow natural equivalents such as alfajiri/asubuhi mapema, migunga/mikakaya for acacia where appropriate, and kuchota/kuteka maji."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:en->sw"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_low","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following sentence to Bengali: 'Climate change is one of the greatest challenges facing humanity today, and addressing it requires cooperation across nations.' Output only the Bengali translation.","ground_truth":["জলবায়ু পরিবর্তন আজ মানবজাতির সামনে থাকা সবচেয়ে বড় চ্যালেঞ্জগুলোর একটি, এবং এর মোকাবিলায় বিভিন্ন দেশের মধ্যে সহযোগিতা প্রয়োজন।","জলবায়ু পরিবর্তন আজ মানবতার সামনে সবচেয়ে বড় চ্যালেঞ্জগুলোর একটি, এবং এটি মোকাবিলা করতে বিভিন্ন দেশের মধ্যে সহযোগিতা প্রয়োজন।","জলবায়ু পরিবর্তন আজ মানবজাতির সামনে থাকা অন্যতম বৃহত্তম চ্যালেঞ্জ, এবং এর মোকাবিলায় বিভিন্ন দেশের মধ্যে সহযোগিতা প্রয়োজন।"],"scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"(?i)^\\s*(?:জলবায়ু\\ পরিবর্তন\\ আজ\\ মানবজাতির\\ সামনে\\ থাকা\\ সবচেয়ে\\ বড়\\ চ্যালেঞ্জগুলোর\\ একটি,\\ এবং\\ এর\\ মোকাবিলায়\\ বিভিন্ন\\ দেশের\\ মধ্যে\\ সহযোগিতা\\ প্রয়োজন।|জলবায়ু\\ পরিবর্তন\\ আজ\\ মানবতার\\ সামনে\\ সবচেয়ে\\ বড়\\ চ্যালেঞ্জগুলোর\\ একটি,\\ এবং\\ এটি\\ মোকাবিলা\\ করতে\\ বিভিন্ন\\ দেশের\\ মধ্যে\\ সহযোগিতা\\ প্রয়োজন।|জলবায়ু\\ পরিবর্তন\\ আজ\\ মানবজাতির\\ সামনে\\ থাকা\\ অন্যতম\\ বৃহত্তম\\ চ্যালেঞ্জ,\\ এবং\\ এর\\ মোকাবিলায়\\ বিভিন্ন\\ দেশের\\ মধ্যে\\ সহযোগিতা\\ প্রয়োজন।)[.?!]?\\s*$"},"tags":["language:en->bn"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L3.003","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_low","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following sentence to Telugu: 'The teacher explained the lesson patiently, drawing diagrams on the blackboard so all students could understand.' Output only the Telugu translation.","ground_truth":"ఉపాధ్యాయుడు పాఠాన్ని ఓపికగా వివరించాడు, విద్యార్థులందరూ అర్థం చేసుకునేలా నల్లబల్లపై రేఖాచిత్రాలు గీశాడు.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"llm_judge","rubric":"判定输出是否为仅包含泰卢固语的英文原句完整译文。应保留以下核心语义：(1) 教师耐心地讲解课程；(2) 教师在黑板上画图/示意图；(3) 此举是为了让所有学生能够理解。允许自然的泰卢固语同义词、语序变化、教师性别或敬语形式变化。若输出只是任意泰卢固字符、无关内容、明显漏掉核心信息、包含解释而非仅译文，则判为不通过。","reference_answers":["ఉపాధ్యాయుడు పాఠాన్ని ఓపికగా వివరించాడు, విద్యార్థులందరూ అర్థం చేసుకునేలా నల్లబల్లపై రేఖాచిత్రాలు గీశాడు.","ఉపాధ్యాయులు పాఠాన్ని ఓపికగా వివరిస్తూ, విద్యార్థులందరికీ అర్థమయ్యేలా నల్లబల్లపై చిత్రాలు గీశారు."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:en->te"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L3.004","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_low","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following sentence into Thai: “Renewable energy sources, such as wind and solar, are key to a sustainable future for our planet.” Output only the Thai translation.","ground_truth":{"reference_answer":"แหล่งพลังงานหมุนเวียน เช่น พลังงานลมและพลังงานแสงอาทิตย์ เป็นกุญแจสำคัญสู่อนาคตที่ยั่งยืนสำหรับโลกของเรา","acceptance_note":"Accept fluent Thai paraphrases that preserve all core meanings: renewable energy sources; wind and solar as examples; their key importance; and a sustainable future for our planet."},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"semantic_rubric","requirements":["Output is predominantly Thai and contains no explanation, source text, or translation label.","Conveys renewable energy sources.","Includes wind and solar as examples, or an unambiguous equivalent construction.","Conveys that these sources are key/important to a sustainable future for our planet.","Allows grammatical and lexical Thai paraphrases."],"reject_if":["The output is merely Thai characters without a complete translation.","Any core meaning is omitted or materially altered.","The output contains commentary or substantial non-translation text."]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:en->th"]}
{"probe_id":"lang.translation_pair.L3.005","canonical_id":"lang.translation_pair","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"pair_resource":"high_low","register":"neutral"},"prompt":"Translate the following sentence into standard Yoruba: “Music has the power to bring people together across cultures and generations.” Output only the Yoruba translation. Diacritics may be included or omitted, but do not add explanation.","ground_truth":{"reference_answers":["Orin ní agbára láti mú àwọn ènìyàn papọ̀ láàárín àwọn àṣà àti àwọn ìran.","Orin ní agbára láti kó àwọn ènìyàn jọ láàárín àwọn àṣà àti àwọn ìran."],"acceptance_note":"接受表达“音乐/歌曲”“有力量/能够”“使人们团结”“跨越/不分文化与世代”的语义等价标准约鲁巴语译文；接受合理的带或不带声调、下加点的正字法变体。"},"scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"llm_rubric","language":"Yoruba","normalize_unicode":true,"rubric":["输出应主要为约鲁巴语，且不得包含解释、英语复述或元评论。","必须表达音乐或歌曲具有力量、能力或作用。","必须表达使人们聚集、团结或联合。","必须表达该作用跨越、不分或涵盖文化和世代两方面。","接受合理同义词、语序差异及带/不带约鲁巴语变音符号的拼写差异。","仅出现音乐、文化、世代或人群等孤立关键词而未表达完整命题时判错。"]}],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["language:en->yo"]}
