{"probe_id":"lang.polarity_clash.L2.004","canonical_id":"lang.polarity_clash","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"polarity_clash_strength":"subtle","context_length":"two_clauses"},"prompt":"Context: A friend cancels plans for the third week in a row. Which sentence is most likely sarcastic? (A) 'I understand, things come up.' (B) 'Wow, you're so reliable.' Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.polarity_clash.L2.005","canonical_id":"lang.polarity_clash","category":"lang","level":"L2","axis_values":{"polarity_clash_strength":"subtle","context_length":"two_clauses"},"prompt":"Context: A restaurant serves soup stone-cold. Which sentence uses sarcasm to criticize how the soup was served? (A) 'They certainly didn't burn it.' (B) 'It's tomato soup.' Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.polarity_clash.L3.001","canonical_id":"lang.polarity_clash","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"polarity_clash_strength":"subtle","context_length":"two_clauses"},"prompt":"After someone has just expressed a very strong opinion, which response is more conventionally sarcastic in everyday English? (A) 'I would love to hear your honest opinion.' (B) 'Oh, tell me how you really feel.' Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"B","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"B"},"tags":[],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"lang.polarity_clash.L3.002","canonical_id":"lang.polarity_clash","category":"lang","level":"L3","axis_values":{"polarity_clash_strength":"context_dependent","context_length":"short_context_plus_two_options"},"prompt":"Context: A teammate promised a report by Friday. On Monday it is still missing, and they ask for another extension. Which reply is more likely sarcastic? (A) 'Your timing continues to be impeccable.' (B) 'Please send it by noon tomorrow.' Reply with one letter.","ground_truth":"A","scorer":{"type":"mcq_letter","expected":"A"},"tags":["sarcasm","pragmatics","polarity_clash"],"notes":""}
